Phase 18 compatibility release gate — response-header identity audit — 2026-10-15 UTC

- Starting revision: `6a3a8671` on `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`; the Java client oracle remains pinned to 5.5.1 commit `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.
- P18-V01 source scan found 16 Rust response-header DTOs deriving structural `PartialEq`/`Eq` whose Java classes inherit `equals/hashCode` from `java.lang.Object`. Added `HeaderResponseIdentityFixtures` to invoke Java reflection for all 16; fixture records the Rust-to-Java class crosswalk, declaring classes, and same/distinct-instance outcomes. Fixture SHA-256: `d618338067333760a74c956d3ca677d4acf0c44acef87b4f9607395fb96f6e6f`.
- Removed the structural equality traits and added compile-fail doctests for all 16 public response headers. Header round-trip tests now compare encoded fields instead of using DTO value equality. The first focused build caught an incorrect fixture include path and five test assertions that depended on response-header `PartialEq`; both were corrected and the complete focused suite passed.
- PASS: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --all-features --locked` (116 unit tests, all integration targets, 41 doctests); strict Protocol all-target/all-feature Clippy; `mvn -q -o -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` (37 scenarios, fixture drift and Java/Rust cross-decodes); `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; `git diff --check`.
- Implementation commit: `79a54e1e fix(compat): preserve response header identity semantics`.
- Next P18-V01 audit item: request headers inheriting `RpcRequestHeader.equals/hashCode` use Java's custom equality over only `ns`, `nsd`, `bname`, and `oway`; the Rust header field models do not yet uniformly represent that inherited state. This and the broader API/input/error/flow/reverse-export audit remain open. Full-workspace P18-V02 rerun, current-revision GitHub Ubuntu evidence, Phase 19 Docker/Broker automation, and release version/registry checks also remain open. No push, tag, publication, or live Broker was used.
